  "name": "Question 20",
  "problem": "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{-6-7\\text{i}}{2\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$",
  "worked_solution": "Here, the denominator is the imaginary number $2\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+2\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-2\\text{i},$ or simply $-2\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-2\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-6-7\\text{i}}{2\\text{i}} & =\\frac{-6-7\\text{i}}{2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-2\\text{i}}{-2\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\text{i}+14{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-4{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\text{i}+14(-1)}{-4(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-14+12\\text{i}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-14+12\\text{i}}{4} & =-\\frac{14}{4}+\\frac{12}{4}\\text{i} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{7}{2})+(3)\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
